cliamp is a retro terminal music player inspired by Winamp 2.x. It plays
local files, internet radio streams, podcasts and online services
(YouTube, SoundCloud, Spotify, Navidrome, Jellyfin, Plex and more), and
offers a spectrum visualizer, a parametric equalizer and a playlist
manager. It exposes an MPRIS D-Bus interface for desktop media keys.

Audio is played through ALSA, which on FreeBSD is routed to OSS by
audio/alsa-plugins.
